-- title:
--   From smooth-point stalks to smooth-point packages at q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and $F$ denotes `fieldBar q M'`, the intermediate field of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}} \subseteq$ `LaurentSeries` $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ obtained by coefficientwise base change from the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$.
--
--   **Data and standing hypotheses.** A prime $q$ with `hq2` : $q = 2$; a nonzero natural number $M'$ with `hqM'` : $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. A valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with `hA` : $A$ lies over $q$, that is, $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa$ for the residue field of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$ with `hW` : the members of $W$ are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. those places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j) \in$ `ssJSet` $q\,\kappa$ for the geometric generator $j =$ `jGeomGen`; and a distinguished element $s$ of $W$. A hypothesis `hle` that `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the base change to $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field) is contained in $F$. A constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa\,M'$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the source together with a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal, pulling back to $A$ along the structure map, compatible with the residue map of $A$, satisfying the scaling property (every nonzero element can be multiplied by a scalar into $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue), and carrying places to places so as to preserve degrees and the orders of nonzero reductions. The hypothesis `hR₀` says that this reduction is coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element belongs to $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, viewed as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **The small-field block.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$; writing $A_0$ for the pullback of $A$ to $k_0$, the hypotheses `hdvr` ($A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring), `hunif` (its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$), `hhens` ($A_0$ is a henselian local ring), `hres` (its residue field is algebraically closed), and `hκ` (every $a \in A$ differs from some element of $k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$).
--
--   **The auxiliary-prime block.** A prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ and such that $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **The layer block.** A type $\iota$, a family $K : \iota \to$ intermediate fields of $k_0 \subseteq \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with each $K_n$ finite-dimensional over $k_0$, and valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ with `hAn` : $x \in A_n$ if and only if $x \in A$ as an element of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Give $F$ the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0 \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\bar{\mathbb{Q}} \to F$. Then, for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0 \subseteq F$ whose compositum with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ is all of $F$, for every field $\mathrm{FSS}$ which is a $\kappa$-algebra, and for every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $F$ to $\mathrm{FSS}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ pulling back to $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto $\mathrm{FSS}$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with the residue map of $A$, and satisfying the scaling property), the following implication holds. For $n \in \iota$ write $F_n$ for the compositum inside $F$ of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_n$ and of $F_0$.
--
--   Both the antecedent and the consequent are conjunctions of the following shape.
--
--   (D) *Drinfeld identification.* For every algebra structure of `GaloisField q 2` on $\kappa$, every witness that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $q\,\kappa$ is a domain, and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$), there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of `GaloisField q 2` and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from $\mathrm{FSS}$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) $q\,\kappa\,C_s$ (the fixed field, inside the Drinfeld function field, of the subgroup generated by the actions of the elements $(1,\zeta)$ with $\zeta \in C_s$) such that $\operatorname{card} C_s =$ `placeWidthChar` $q\,M'\,s$ (for $q = 2$: $12$ or $1$ according as $s$ has $j$-invariant $0$ or not, divided by the $j$-ramification index of $s$), and such that $e$ intertwines the two actions: for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every witness that `levelAutBar` $q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and every witness that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), the image of $e(R.\mathrm{resAut}(\text{levelAutBar } q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1})\,x)$ in the Drinfeld function field equals the action of $\langle(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)\rangle$ through `hFunctionFieldAction` on the image of $e(x)$, for all $x \in \mathrm{FSS}$.
--
--   Together with (D) there exist a finite set $N$ of places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\kappa$, subrings $S_{Q,n} \subseteq F$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_{Q,n} : A_n[X] \to S_{Q,n}$ and $\chi_{Q,n} : S_{Q,n} \to \kappa$, and sets $D_{Q,n}$ of places of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, indexed by such places $Q$ and by $n \in \iota$, such that:
--
--   (N) $\operatorname{card} N = q+1$;
--
--   (B) *affine chart.* there is a subring $B \subseteq F$ with $B \subseteq R.\mathrm{integers}$, with $B \subseteq S_{Q,n}$ for all $Q \notin N$ and all $n$, and such that every $z \in \mathrm{FSS}$ lying in the valuation subring of every $Q \notin N$ is the $R$-residue of some $f \in B$;
--
--   (L) for every $Q \notin N$ and every $n \in \iota$, the layer clauses listed below hold;
--
--   (M) *monotonicity.* for every $Q \notin N$ there is a witness `hmono` that $K_n \le K_{n'}$ implies $S_{Q,n} \subseteq S_{Q,n'}$, and moreover: $K_n \le K_{n'}$ implies that $S_{Q,n'}$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_{Q,n}$ together with the images of $A_{n'}$; the element $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ of $F$ is the same for all $n, n'$; and $\chi_{Q,n'}$ restricted along `hmono` agrees with $\chi_{Q,n}$;
--
--   (Sep) *separation.* if $Q, Q' \notin N$, $n \in \iota$ and a place $P$ of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies both in $D_{Q,n}$ and in $D_{Q',n}$, then $Q = Q'$;
--
--   (J) for $Q \notin N$, $n \in \iota$ and $P \in D_{Q,n}$, one has $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the element of $F$ obtained, via `hle`, from the coefficientwise image in Laurent series over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the $q$-expansion `jq` of the modular invariant;
--
--   (Eq) *equivariance.* for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphisms of $F$ generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar` $q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every witness that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$: for every place $Q$ of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\kappa$ one has $R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau) \cdot Q \in N$ if and only if $Q \in N$, and if $Q \notin N$ then for every $n$ the translate `smulDisc` $\tau\,(D_{Q,n}) = \{P : \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D_{Q,n}\}$ equals $D_{R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q,\,n}$.
--
--   **Antecedent layer clauses (stalks).** For $Q \notin N$ and $n \in \iota$: (1) the map sending $a \in A_n$ to the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$ is surjective; (2) the image in $F$ of every $a \in A_n$ lies in $S_{Q,n}$; (3) $\varphi_{Q,n}$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; (4) $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a)$ is, in $F$, the image of $a$; (5) $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; (6) $\chi_{Q,n}(\varphi_{Q,n}(X)) = 0$; (7) for every $c \in A_n$ with residue $0$ there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi : S_{Q,n} \to A_n$ with $\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,a)) = a$ for all $a$, with the residue of $\chi(f)$ equal to $\chi_{Q,n}(f)$ for all $f$, and with $\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(X)) = c$; (8) every $f \in S_{Q,n}$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there is the image of $\chi_{Q,n}(f)$ under $\kappa \to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; (9) $Q.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $R$-residue of $\varphi_{Q,n}(X)$ equals $1$; (10) a place $P$ lies in $D_{Q,n}$ if and only if $P$ is rational, every $f \in S_{Q,n}$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for every $f$ one has $A.\mathrm{valuation}(P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)) < 1$ exactly when $\chi_{Q,n}(f) = 0$; (11) $\varphi_{Q,n}(X) \ne \varphi_{Q,n}(C\,c)$ for every $c \in A_n$; (12) $S_{Q,n}$ is a local ring whose maximal ideal is the zero set of $\chi_{Q,n}$, and is Noetherian and a unique factorisation domain; (13) $S_{Q,n} \subseteq F_n$; (14) every $f \in F_n$ satisfies $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_{Q,n}$ with $h \ne 0$; (15) if $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ is linearly independent over $K_n$ and $a_i \in F_n$ satisfy $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ in $F$, then all $a_i = 0$; (16) every ring homomorphism $\chi : S_{Q,n} \to A_n$ satisfying the two compatibilities of (7) has kernel the ideal generated by $\varphi_{Q,n}(X) - \varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\chi(\varphi_{Q,n}(X)))$; (17) there is a generator $\varpi$ of the maximal ideal of $A_n$, nonzero, such that $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi)$ is prime in $S_{Q,n}$, such that an element $f \in F_n$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ precisely when $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_{Q,n}$ with $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi) \nmid h$, and such that for every prime $p$ of $S_{Q,n}$ not associated to $\varphi_{Q,n}(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x \in S_{Q,n}$ there is a monic $r \in A_n[X]$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of $r$ pushed forward along $\varphi_{Q,n} \circ C$; (18) there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_{Q,n}$ such that every $f \in S_{Q,n}$ satisfies $f h = g$ with $g, h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the images of $A_n$, and with $h$ the image of a unit of $S_{Q,n}$.
--
--   **Consequent layer clauses (packages).** For $Q \notin N$ and $n \in \iota$, clauses (1)–(10) above, and in addition: (11′) for every ring homomorphism $\chi : S_{Q,n} \to A_n$ satisfying the two compatibilities of (7) there is a unique place $P$ with $P \in D_{Q,n}$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) = \chi(f)$ in $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ for all $f \in S_{Q,n}$; (12′) for every $P \in D_{Q,n}$ and every $f \in F_n$, $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in S_{Q,n}$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(h) \ne 0$; (13′) *unit principle*: if $f \in F_n$ is nonzero and $P.\mathrm{ord}(f) = 0$ for all $P \in D_{Q,n}$, then there are a nonzero $c \in K_n$ and a unit $u$ of $S_{Q,n}$ with $c f = u$ in $F$; (14′) if $f \in F_n$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and in the valuation subring of every $P \in D_{Q,n}$, then $f \in S_{Q,n}$; (15′) the finite-generation clause (18) above.
--
--   Thus the implication keeps the Drinfeld identification, the cardinality of $N$, the affine-chart subring $B$, the monotonicity, separation, $j$-order and equivariance clauses unchanged, replaces the stalk-theoretic clauses (11), (12), (13), (14), (15), (16), (17) of each layer by the disc-theoretic clauses (11′)–(14′), and re-asserts the existence of data $N, S, \varphi, \chi, D$ with these properties.
--
--   This is the functorial step of the supersingular column at $q = 2$ over a rigid auxiliary level: it upgrades, uniformly in the auxiliary field $F_0$ and in the regular prolongation $R$, the local (stalk) description of the smooth points of the special fibre at each layer $K_n$ — local ring $S_{Q,n}$, uniformiser, unique factorisation, section kernels — to the package description in terms of residue discs $D_{Q,n}$: a bijection between sections and points of the disc, locality of membership in the valuation subrings, the unit principle and the criterion for membership in $S_{Q,n}$. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart) in the construction of the semistable model of the modular curve at a supersingular point in characteristic $2$.
